{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on `3c5b8265`: the call shape and the paths are accepted.\nApply them. The five answers:\n\n1. Recompute at the view, for both forms. `now` has one meaning:\n   the basis that this view renders. A stored cut can be older\n   than the row on the page. Then the member sees the row at 41,\n   passes a stored 40, and gets a second return for a row that the\n   page already showed. That is an extra submit, and the owner\n   ruled it out. So the stored draft of form 1 keeps its basis and\n   the cause, as form 2 does, and the view computes the movement\n   and `now` from the kept basis and the rows that it holds. If a\n   reader other than the view needs the stored movement, name it\n   before you remove the field.\n2. Yes, `state`. A view that cannot render a subject gives no\n   `now`, and a submit stops before any signature. The view says\n   which subject it lacks, so a page can tell the member. Edit and\n   `dismiss` still work, and `now` appears when the replica holds\n   the row.\n3. Yes. On MCP, `after` with `now` is the submit of a returned\n   request. A bare `act` is a fresh act with its own key.\n4. On every refused result that a model can answer with `after`.\n   One rule for each cause, as in the client.\n5. Confirmed. A refusal by the scope after a passed exploration\n   returns the draft with a new `now`, and the member submits one\n   time more. No hidden retry, ever: a retry signs on a row that\n   the member has not seen. Each real race costs one submit.\n\nTwo conditions:\n- One generated case in the existing owner: a row that moves\n  between each pair of steps of return, view and submit. The\n  member never signs on a subject that no passed `now` named, and\n  one race costs one submit.\n- The implementation note states the limit of an MCP host that\n  drops tool output: the model gets `shape` and can send a fresh\n  act.\n\nThe seventh amendment takes item 1 into section 6: a return has\none stored shape and two causes.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}